LOGBOOK.md:1136:### 2113 — A gate must prove its own coverage; so must a mutation sweep
LOGBOOK.md:1140:- ANOMALY: The mutation harness aborted mid-run on the zsh reserved variable `status`, after applying mutant 1 but before its restore. The next run took its baseline backup from that mutated tree, so all 12 mutants were behavioural no-ops against an already-red mask and every one reported KILLED for the wrong reason. Caught only because the full-repo run afterwards failed.
LOGBOOK.md:1144:- NOTE: General property, applies to every derived gate — an inventory must assert that the set of constructs it scans is complete for the package, and a mutation sweep must assert its baseline is green. A gate that cannot fail when someone adds a second copy of a check is decoration, and a mutant that "kills" an already-red mask proves nothing.
LOGBOOK.md:1156:- DECISION: Row resolution is detail-mention OR (entry-mention AND wire-or-verified-predicate-mention), with predicates verified from the production AST. External tests assert codes through predicates with isolating fixtures; demanding detail strings there would misdescribe the battery. Misattribution (right detail, wrong test) remains a review finding — three such rows were caught by reading the generated table, not by the gate.
